	"comments": [
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xelkj5g5tyniwkaxkxzi5hhj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz6udnp3dc2n",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lynn.zone/post/3lz6udnp3dc2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "Lynn",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lynn.zone",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xelkj5g5tyniwkaxkxzi5hhj/bafkreiemxndhhqdq33kfkcntxm55rtxyyrhs4ubynlmh22zlglrfaixs7e"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-19T12:26:11.658Z",
			"content": "<p>`scrollbar-gutter` is great, but I don't know if I'd go so far as to argue that everyone should be putting it in their resets. As far as I'm aware, there's currently no way to put *anything* in the space it reserves, which unfortunately makes it awkward to use with some pretty common layouts</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7g6egal4g5xxyndeeltr5oss/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz6vqcbsgc2c",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mayank.co/post/3lz6vqcbsgc2c",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2025-09-19T12:51:09.581Z",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:343p6xcgmvkpz5abgezlgyep/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz6zkbc42s2m",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us/post/3lz6zkbc42s2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Bramus",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:343p6xcgmvkpz5abgezlgyep/bafkreigkuhuvdn6qvnizxa3agd26bvtkc7xmw5uqjnyh3g4zun4bxhzrsq"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-19T13:59:22.240Z",
			"content": "<p>As long as you don’t go for `scrollbar-gutter: stable both-edges`, you should be fine.</p>\n<p>Reason: Chrome has a bug in which the gutter is doubled up on “retina” devices: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40064879\">issues.chromium.org/issues/40064...</a></p>\n<p>(The bug is assigned, and I heard engineering will look at it next quarter)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:343p6xcgmvkpz5abgezlgyep/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz6znkz6u22m",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xelkj5g5tyniwkaxkxzi5hhj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz6udnp3dc2n",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us/post/3lz6znkz6u22m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Bramus",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:343p6xcgmvkpz5abgezlgyep/bafkreigkuhuvdn6qvnizxa3agd26bvtkc7xmw5uqjnyh3g4zun4bxhzrsq"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-19T14:01:13.097Z",
			"content": "<p>There’s still some discussion on how viewports should behave in this case.</p>\n<p>What the WG did resolve on – but this hasn’t been implemented anywhere (😔) – is that top layer content (such as a modal dialog and its backdrop, or a fullscreen video) can draw on top of the reserved space.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
