			"date": "2025-09-30T21:59:13.542Z",
			"content": "<p>Curiosity - what layouts do you mean? The site layouts I see daily would not be hindered/made awkward by having space reserved for the vertical scrollbar. The only way I can see that being an issue is if the layout is a side-scrolling layout, but I haven't seen one of those in years.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xelkj5g5tyniwkaxkxzi5hhj/app.bsky.feed.post/3m23k4tgwps2d",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:7le3gpdvacl6bx2zfg62k2vc/app.bsky.feed.post/3m23jigv6vk24",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lynn.zone/post/3m23k4tgwps2d",
			"author": {
				"name": "Lynn",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lynn.zone",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xelkj5g5tyniwkaxkxzi5hhj/bafkreiemxndhhqdq33kfkcntxm55rtxyyrhs4ubynlmh22zlglrfaixs7e"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-30T22:10:37.795Z",
			"content": "<p>Any layout with elements that are meant to span the whole width of the (scrollable) container will run into this problem. Navbars, list dividers, etc.</p>\n<p>Things like backdrops for dialogs are also affected, but I guess you could argue those are less of a big deal.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xhhcrzsilpamjmz4dvrpt7df/app.bsky.feed.post/3m77ha7fawc2s",
